   "Section C: Fast Multiplication (Karatsuba)",
   [
    "a) 1011 \u00d7 1101 (4-bit): split X = 10|11, Y = 11|01 (halves of 2 bits)",
    "  z2 = Xh\u00b7Yh = 10 \u00d7 11 = 110 (6);  z0 = Xl\u00b7Yl = 11 \u00d7 01 = 11 (3)",
    "  z1 = (Xh + Xl)(Yh + Yl) - z2 - z0 = (101)(100) - 110 - 11 = 10100 - 1001 = 1011 (11)",
    "  Product = z2\u00b72^4 + z1\u00b72^2 + z0 = 1100000 + 101100 + 11 = 10001111 = 143   (11 \u00d7 13 = 143 \u2713)",
    "b) 54 \u00d7 87: 54 = 00110110, 87 = 01010111 (8-bit); split into 4-bit halves: Xh = 0011 (3), Xl = 0110 (6), Yh = 0101 (5), Yl = 0111 (7)",
    "  z2 = 3 \u00d7 5 = 15;  z0 = 6 \u00d7 7 = 42;  z1 = (3 + 6)(5 + 7) - 15 - 42 = 9 \u00d7 12 - 57 = 108 - 57 = 51",
    "  Product = 15 \u00d7 256 + 51 \u00d7 16 + 42 = 3840 + 816 + 42 = 4698   (54 \u00d7 87 = 4698 \u2713)",
    "  In binary: 4698 = 1001001011010",
    "c) X = 11011011, Y = 10111001 setup: Xh = 1101, Xl = 1011, Yh = 1011, Yl = 1001",
